  "structural_proof": [
    "Use the fixed complex embedding zeta42=exp(2*pi*i/42). The quadratic Gauss sum s7 defined here is i*sqrt(7): its square is -7 by exact cyclotomic reduction; the standard odd quadratic Gauss-sum sign or direct sine signs select positive imaginary part. The exact identity sqrt21=-s3*s7 and positive identity embedding of sqrt21, together with s3=i*sqrt(3), independently fixes s7=i*sqrt(7).",
    "For real embeddings indexed by r=1,5,11,13,17,19, s7 transforms by the quadratic character chi_-7(r). The selected CM embedding is r if r lies in Phi and -r otherwise. A trace alternating form E_xi(x,y)=Tr_M/Q(xi*x*bar(y)) has E_xi(x,Jx)>0 when the imaginary part of phi(xi) is positive for each phi in Phi. The certified b-sign equals chi_-7(r) times the selection sign; hence xi=s7*b has positive imaginary part in all selected CM embeddings.",
    "Take the complex torus C^6/Phi(O_M). Since b and s7 are algebraic integers, E_xi is integral on O_M; xi is nonzero and conjugate(xi)=-xi, so E_xi is a nondegenerate alternating form. It is J-invariant and positive in the stated convention. Thus it is a polarization, giving an abelian sixfold with this abstract CM type. Scaling by a positive integer works for any commensurable lattice; no principal polarization is claimed.",
    "The K-action satisfies E_xi(kx,ky)=Nm_K/Q(k)*E_xi(x,y). The character fibers each contain three selected type embeddings, so the K-signature is (3,3). Let T(x,y)=Tr_M/K(b*x*bar(y)). Then the Hermitian form E_xi(s7*x,y)+s7*E_xi(x,y) equals -14*T(x,y), by expanding the quadratic trace. This is compatible with the same polarization; the factor (-14)^6 in rank six is a rational square and hence a K-norm.",
    "The vectors 1,t,...,t^5 form a K-basis of M. Indeed L is totally real and K imaginary quadratic, so L and K are linearly disjoint over Q and M=LK. On this basis T has entries Tr_L/Q(b*t^(i+j)). Its determinant is disc(1,t,...,t^5)*N_L/Q(b), a standard trace-pairing change-of-multiplication determinant identity.",
    "Every t_a is a Galois conjugate of t and N(t)=1 from the constant term of its degree-six minimal polynomial. Thus N(u)=1. The positive sqrt21 generates the real quadratic subfield and has three conjugates +sqrt21 and three -sqrt21, giving norm -21^3. Consequently det(T)=-3^6*7^8=-(3^3*7^4)^2. Explicitly (3^3*7^4)^2 is Nm_K/Q(3^3*7^4), so the Hermitian discriminant class is -1.",
    "The construction concerns a rational CM Hodge structure and a freely chosen compatible polarization. It supplies no statement that the standard trace polarization on a marked McMullen fiber has this determinant or is principal. For another variety of this abstract CM type with rational M-action, an M-linear identification H1(A,Q)=M transports the rational alternating form; clearing denominators makes it an integral polarization. The positivity depends only on the CM type and is unaffected by choosing a different commensurable lattice.",
    "If independently accepted, these hypotheses meet Markman Theorem 1.5.1 for K=Q(sqrt(-7)); the previously reviewed all-powers invariant-generation lemma would then give Hodge algebraicity for every power of this abstract isogeny type. This preparation does not itself promote that consequence."
  ]
